      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 816,
        "content": "## Generate an AI Video from an Image with img2.video (Grok Imagine, Kling 2.6, Veo 3)\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow manually starts an image-to-video generation job with img2.video using a configured image URL, model ID, prompt, and API base URL. It submits the job, waits in 20-second intervals, polls the job status, and loops until the generation succeeds. When the video is ready, it outputs the resulting video URL.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Add the required img2.video API credential or API key to the HTTP Request nodes, typically as an authorization header.\n- Update the Config node with your source imageUrl, desired modelId, prompt, and baseUrl values.\n- Verify the Submit Job node sends the request body expected by the img2.video generation endpoint.\n- Confirm the Poll Job and Succeeded? nodes reference the correct job ID, status field, and success condition from the API response.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the modelId to switch between supported video models such as Grok Imagine, Kling 2.6, or Veo 3. Adjust the prompt, image URL, polling interval, and success condition to match your preferred generation behavior and API response format."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3c5cdb39-391b-41d7-a9b1-28f22d0679b3",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
